{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_015 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.6186 acc, only ~2.8% above RNA-only (config_013, 0.5907), while image-only (config_023) is very weak at 0.3275. This suggests the image modality contributes little, likely because ResNet50 is a relatively weak encoder for cellular images. Question: config_002 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (keeping pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, concat identical to config_015), directly testing whether a stronger image representation unlocks more signal for fusion. Why best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against config_015, isolating the effect of image representation quality. If ViT-L substantially improves the multimodal model, it confirms the image encoder was the bottleneck and justifies further investment in image-side design (aggregation, fusion). If it does not, it indicates the image modality itself is limited regardless of encoder strength, redirecting effort toward RNA encoders or profile settings. Under a tight budget, this single experiment resolves a high-uncertainty question about whether the image branch is worth further optimization."
}

